{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>For it is no empty thing for you.</b> Not for nothing do you toil in it — for much reward depends on it; <b>for it is your life.</b> Another interpretation — there is nothing empty in the Torah, that if you expound it there is no giving of reward in it. Know for yourself that so the Sages said: \"וַאֲחוֹת לוֹטָן תִּמְנָע\" (Genesis 36) — \"וְתִמְנַע הָיְתָה פִילֶגֶשׁ\" etc. — because she said, 'I am not worthy to be his wife; would that I be his concubine.' And all this, why? To make known the praise of Abraham, that rulers and kings long to attach themselves to his seed (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:32.449762232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}